  "implementation": [
    "Preflight includes every emitted profile ring, exact square/round shell index counts and both end faces before emitting geometry. Vertex and native indexed-draw counts must fit u32.",
    "Ring and cap offsets propagate PackingError::IndexOverflow instead of silently returning or saturating.",
    "Shared structure/glycan trace generation clears all emitted vertex/index/deformation columns when a trace fails; the renderer propagates the typed failure and does not upload incomplete geometry.",
    "Low-level RibbonMesh generate/generate_styled/generate_glycan now return Result. All callers migrate. The facade, command, Python and WASM specifications are unchanged.",
    "Index reservation uses the already-checked actual shell count, including flat intervals. No extra allocation or GPU upload is added to steady-state camera-only rendering."
  ],
  "invariants": {
    "tests": "crates/molgfx-geometry/src/cartoon/draw_limits_tests.rs",
    "facts": [
      "A sweep just above the vertex limit fails with its rejected exact offset. The adjacent boundary succeeds.",
      "A sweep just above the native index-count limit fails; its adjacent boundary succeeds.",
      "Flat shells/caps use their exact counts, without pessimistic round-shell rejection.",
      "Arithmetic overflow returns a typed failure instead of wrapping."
    ],
    "limitation": "Boundary tests exercise checked arithmetic without allocating a multi-billion-vertex mesh. They do not claim an actual multi-billion-vertex GPU render."
  },
  "complexity": "An additional allocation-free O(samples) preflight runs only when a cached ribbon is regenerated. Extrusion remains O(guides + samples), with O(samples) output memory. Camera-only cached rendering is unchanged.",
